## Standard

This repository follows [dashboards-as-code v1.1.0](https://github.com/opsdevcode/repave/blob/main/standards/observability/dashboards-as-code.md)
(RED / golden signals, OpenTelemetry-style tags, Grafana and Datadog best practices).

## Layout

{% if backend == 'grafana' %}
- `grafana/dashboards/service-overview.json` — context, links, ownership
- `grafana/dashboards/service-golden-signals.json` — golden signals baseline (rate, errors, duration)
{% if dashboard_pack_source != 'repave-red-starter' %}
- Additional JSON from community pack **{{ dashboard_pack_source }}** (see `observability/catalog.json`)
{% endif %}
{% elif backend == 'datadog' %}
- `datadog/dashboards/service-overview.json` — context note widget
- `datadog/dashboards/service-golden-signals.json` — golden signals baseline widgets
{% endif %}

## Usage

{% if backend == 'grafana' %}
Import JSON from `grafana/dashboards/` via Grafana UI/API or GitOps (Grafana Operator,
`grafonnet`, Terraform `grafana_dashboard` / JSON resource).
{% elif backend == 'datadog' %}
Import JSON via [Datadog dashboard API](https://docs.datadoghq.com/api/latest/dashboards/),
Terraform `datadog_dashboard_json`, or your internal GitOps pipeline.
{% endif %}
On-call should start from **service-overview** and **service-golden-signals** before custom panels.

## Validate locally

Regenerate or publish through repave; `grafana-dashboard` / `datadog-dashboard` gates
validate JSON and required tags when dashboard files are present.

## Provenance

Generation metadata lives in `repave.yaml`. The `provenance-drift` gate validates it on
every generate/publish.
